&lt;/span>
&lt;/h1>
&lt;p>When running an &lt;a
href="https://ipfs.tech/"
target="_blank"
>IPFS&lt;/a> node, one of the most important security considerations is how you handle &lt;strong>ports&lt;/strong> and the &lt;strong>RPC API&lt;/strong>. Many new users unknowingly expose their node’s RPC API to the internet, leaving it wide open for abuse. In this post, we’ll explore why this is dangerous and how you can protect yourself with IPFS’s built-in &lt;strong>basic authentication&lt;/strong>.&lt;/p></description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://yalchin403.github.io/blog/posts/how-to-secure-ipfs-node/featured.png"/></item></channel></rss>